          "ruleId": "t1-guard-baseline-held-fix-verified",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Fix verified. With a mutated autopilot (INT/TERM trap deleted) the baseline case fails and every one of the 11 mutants still runs and prints its line before the verdict: report mode exits 0 with FAIL, REPORT lines after the mutants, ENFORCE=1 exits 1, ENV is rc 2 in both modes. A moved mutant anchor on a green tree gives rc 0 with REPORT and rc 1 under ENFORCE. On the real tree the guard passes 8 cases and 11 of 11 mutants (rc 0) and now ends in finish 0."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "scripts/check_release_t1_lanes_joined.sh"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 146
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "measured",
            "command": [
              "bash",
              "scripts/check_release_t1_lanes_joined.sh",
              "<mutated autopilot>"
            ],
            "exit_code": 0,
            "stdout_sha256": "e0fa2fd71b826289beaa3bf3f8e11c6bf539f846772fe7f6435765114655ba6b",
            "failure_scenario": "none: the previous finding is closed.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "t1-guard-kills-vacuous-on-red-baseline",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "When the baseline is red, the mutants are all judged on the same broken tree, so every one that is applied is reported killed. Measured: on the no-trap autopilot the report shows 10 'ok mutant ... killed' lines under a failed baseline. The verdict is still FAIL, so nothing passes wrongly, but those kill lines are not evidence that the case table catches the mutants, and a surviving mutant is masked until the baseline is green (the same shape the author's fix removed for hiding). Fix: print the kill lines only when the baseline is green, or tag them 'not judged (baseline red)'."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "scripts/check_release_t1_lanes_joined.sh"
                },
                "region": {
