          "ruleId": "agy-mutant-killed-by-red-baseline",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Mutants are incorrectly counted as killed if the baseline fails."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "scripts/check_release_t1_lanes_joined.sh"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 148
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "asserted",
            "rationale": "agy mark measured. Re-marked asserted: agy supplied no command or stdout digest. The primary reproduced it (t1-guard-kills-vacuous-on-red-baseline), so it is agreed.",
            "failure_scenario": "If the baseline validation fails (`bad=1`), the `check` function will also fail for all mutants because they are based on the same broken baseline. The `mutant()` function interprets any `check` failure as the mutant being 'killed', which artificially inflates the kill count and masks surviving mutants.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "agy-inverted-exits",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "There are inverted exits present in the validation logic."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "scripts/check_release_t1_lanes_joined.sh"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 40
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "asserted",
            "rationale": "agy mark asserted, with no location or detail. CONTRADICTED by the primary: report mode exits 0, ENFORCE=1 exits 1 and ENV exits 2, measured on a mutated autopilot, a moved anchor and a missing autopilot. No inverted exit exists.",
            "failure_scenario": "Exit conditions or logic checks evaluate inversely to their intended boolean logic, causing the script to either exit with an incorrect status or produce false positives/negatives during validation.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "agy-paths-skip-finish",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "The success path skips the finish function."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "scripts/check_release_t1_lanes_joined.sh"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 173
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "asserted",
            "rationale": "agy mark cited. The finding describes the code before this patch; the patch adds finish 0 at the end, so the point is resolved, not open.",
            "failure_scenario": "Before the patch, the script's success path reached EOF and exited implicitly with code 0 without calling the `finish` function, bypassing the centralized exit logic and reporting. The patch resolves this by adding `finish 0` at the end of the script.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        }
